            "Tetragonal system. Bipyramidal crystals resembling octahedra, sometimes tabular; granular masses. Distinct cleavage; uneven to conchoidal fracture. Hardness 4.5 to 5; specific gravity 5.9 to 6.1, very heavy; adamantine to vitreous lustre; refractive index 1.918 to 1.937; birefringence 0.016 to 0.017 (uniaxial positive); dispersion 0.026, comparable to diamond, hence lively fire. Bright blue fluorescence under short-wave UV, used by prospectors to locate it at night. Too soft for everyday wear, it is a collector's gem.",
